<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Select Box</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p>This command is accessible from <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Select &gt; Box</b></span>.</p>
<p class="description"><span lang="EN-GB" class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Select Box</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command selects these visible points that are located in a specific</span> box defined by minimum and maximum co-ordinates in <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>X</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Y</b></span>, and <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Z</b></span>. <span lang="EN-GB">This command is applied only to compound entities  scan data, meshes, point clouds, polylines, and static stripes. When called</span> <span class="Command">Select Box</span> <span lang="EN-GB">displays the extents of all visible compound entities according to the current viewport.</span></p>
<table class="TableGrid" style="border-collapse:collapse; border-spacing:0px;" cellspacing="0">
<tr>
<td valign="top" class="whs4">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../images/select_box.gif" width="219px" height="324px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td class="whs6">
<ul class="whs7">
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:19px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>MaxX</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"> left end of the extents in relation to the viewport.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:19px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>MinX</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"> right end of the extents in relation to the viewport.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:19px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>MaxY</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"> top end of the extents in relation to the viewport.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:19px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>MinY</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"> bottom end of the extents in relation to the viewport.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:19px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>MaxZ</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"> near end of the extents in relation to the viewport.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:19px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>MinZ</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"> far end of the extents in relation to the viewport.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This selection tool is a mode, which means that it will stay on the left pane until you close it. During this time you can rotate, pan, and zoom the viewport in order to achieve better observation of the objects and extents box (which ends are marked with yellow lines.)</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Example</u></span></a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP160409102" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table cellspacing="0" class="whs8">
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs9">
<td class="whs10">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/select_box_2.gif" width="250px" height="250px" border="0" class="img_whs11" alt=""></span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB">Using spin buttons in the dialog you can adjust the extents of the selection that you want to make. You can check at any time whether the selection satisfies you simply by pressing Select button.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/select_box_3.gif" width="259px" height="250px" border="0" class="img_whs12" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>&#160;</p>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">When you are ready, press</span> <span class="Button">Close</span> <span lang="EN-GB">button to exit</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Box Selection</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">dialog. Note that</span> <span class="Command">Select Box</span> <span lang="EN-GB">removes any previous selections of compound data. Datum entities remain unaffected.</span></p>
<p class="Use"><span class="Command">Select Box</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>useful</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">when editing data with known lines of symmetry in body co-ordinates.&#160;</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Related topic:</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"><a href="Rectangular_Selection.htm">Rectangular Selection</a></span></p>

